<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    <title>Math Calendar {{year}}</title>

    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Math Calendar {{year}}" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Daily Epsilon calendar problems and solutions for {{year}}." />

    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/mathstyles.css" />
    <script type="text/javascript" src="/mathscripts.js" defer></script>

    <style type="text/css">
        #cal {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px,1fr));
            gap: 10px;
        }
        #cal table {
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 250px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            text-align: center;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="root">

<h1>Math Calendar {{year}}</h1>

<p>
These problems are from <a href="https://dailyepsilon.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
<em>Your Daily Epsilon of Math</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
Problems are organized into monthly pages. Click on the month name to see the
page for that month, or a specific date to go right to a particular problem.
</p>

<p>
There are various ways in which the problem can ask for a solution. If they do
not state what to solve for in words, it may be the value of x, the value of a
mathematical expression, or the area of a shaded region for geometry problems.
</p>

<div id="cal">

{% for month_table,month_full,month_link in data %}
<table class="mathcal_month_table">
    <tr><th colspan="7"><a href="{{month_link}}">{{month_full}}</a></th></tr>
    <tr>
        <th scope="col">Mo</th>
        <th scope="col">Tu</th>
        <th scope="col">We</th>
        <th scope="col">Th</th>
        <th scope="col">Fr</th>
        <th scope="col">Sa</th>
        <th scope="col">Su</th>
    </tr>
    {% for week_row in month_table %}
    <tr>
        {% for text,link in week_row %}
        {% if link %}
        <td><a href="{{link}}" aria-label="{{month_full}} {{text}}">{{text}}</a></td>
        {% else %}
        <td>{{text}}</td>
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
</table>

{% endfor %}
</div><!-- end cal -->

</div><!-- end root -->
</body>
</html>
